    "lineage": [
      "12-COUNCIL-PROTOCOLS-AND-PRESETS.md#P11",
      "US IC Team A / Team B 1976"
    ],
    "notes": "ADVERSARIAL. Full independent RE-DERIVATION from raw sources, which is what separates it from a red team attacking an existing artifact. The two cells are real nested CouncilSpec instances under topology.subcouncils, each validated by the same schema and the same semantic rules; nesting is capped at one level.\n\nanti-failure controls, each mapped to the field implementing it:\n  echo_chamber -> two fully independent cells (topology.subcouncils) re-derive the estimate from the same pinned raw sources; neither sees the other's product until adjudication\n  collusion -> the card's failure mode is Team B leaking Team A's framing through a shared brief, so the brief must be byte-identical and conclusion-free: custom:brief_hash_identical == true AND custom:team_a_tokens_in_team_b_brief == 0 are both closing preconditions\n  hidden_conflict_of_interest -> participants.conflicts_policy.on_conflict=recuse_from_vote with disclosure_required, applied to the adjudication panel that sees both products\n  evidence_free_majority -> voting.method=judge with evidence_gate.evidence_outranks_majority; a divergence is settled by the sources, not by which cell had more seats\n  premature_convergence -> topology.fan_in.require_all_subcouncils_complete + the subcouncils_complete >= 2 conjunct; adjudication cannot start on one cell's answer"
  }
